          {
            "kind": "term",
            "id": "check",
            "text": "jaques"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": ", las capturas y las amenazas. Un jaque obliga a salir del jaque; una captura casi obliga a recapturar; una amenaza obliga a defenderse. Antes de elegir jugada, mira primero las tuyas, en ese orden: jaques, capturas y amenazas. Aquí las blancas tienen dos jaques, los de las flechas."
          }
        ],
        "en": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "A "
          },
          {
            "kind": "term",
            "id": "forcing-move",
            "text": "forcing move"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " leaves the rival few answers. There are three kinds: "
          },
          {
            "kind": "term",
            "id": "check",
            "text": "checks"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": ", captures and threats. A check must be answered by getting out of check; a capture almost forces a recapture; a threat forces a defence. Before choosing a move, look at yours first, in that order: checks, captures and threats. Here White has two checks, the ones on the arrows."
          }
        ]
      },
